#
# The boot command for the Buildroot image, served by the TFTP server and
# fetched by the one line the card carries.  Edit here, copy to /srv/tftp,
# reset the board; the card is never touched.
#
# WHAT IT DOES.  The CADR goes into the fabric first: `fpga loadb` configures
# it with cadr.bit and the machine is running its boot PROM out of DDR3
# before the kernel is fetched.  Then the tree, the kernel and the root
# filesystem, all three from the server, and `bootz` with all three --- a
# zImage, a U-Boot ramdisk image (rootfs.cpio.uboot, the initramfs), and a
# raw tree.  The addresses are U-Boot's environment's, set and explained in
# linux/buildroot/board/arty-z7-20/uboot/cadr.env.
#
# WHAT IS NOT ON THE COMMAND LINE, against the stepping stone's.  No
# `mem=384M`: the tree's reserved-memory node, `no-map`, is what keeps this
# kernel off the CADR's region, and whether it does is one of the two things
# the first boot of this image is to establish (docs/boot.md, "The Buildroot
# image").  No `cma=32M`: nothing here allocates from CMA and the kernel's
# pool is the default.  No `uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id`: there are no PL
# peripherals in the tree.  `earlycon` with no argument takes the console
# from the tree's stdout-path.
#
# WHAT IS NOT DONE HERE.  fdt_high and initrd_high are left unset: U-Boot
# relocates the tree and the ramdisk into memory it allocates below its own,
# and the reserved-memory node in its tree keeps that below the CADR's
# region.  If either is ever set to 0xffffffff the blobs stay where they were
# loaded, which is also below it.
netcmd=tftpboot ${cadr_bit_addr} cadr.bit && fpga loadb 0 ${cadr_bit_addr} ${filesize} && tftpboot ${cadr_fdt_addr} zynq-arty-z7-20.dtb && tftpboot ${cadr_kernel_addr} zImage && tftpboot ${cadr_ramdisk_addr} rootfs.cpio.uboot && setenv bootargs console=ttyPS0,115200 earlycon && bootz ${cadr_kernel_addr} ${cadr_ramdisk_addr} ${cadr_fdt_addr}
